coder › Implemented `wrap(text, width)` in `src/wrap.ts` and added tests in `src/wrap.test.ts`.

What changed:
- `wrap` now:
  - throws `RangeError` when `width` is below 1 (the `!(width >= 1)` guard also catches `NaN`)
  - splits input into paragraphs on blank lines (empty or whitespace-only)
  - collapses runs of whitespace within a paragraph into a single separator
  - greedily fills lines up to `width` characters, breaking at spaces
  - splits words longer than `width` into `width`-sized chunks
  - joins paragraph blocks with exactly one blank line between them
  - never leaves a trailing space on a line
- Added 13 tests covering the documented behavior plus edge cases (multiple blank lines, leading/trailing blank lines, whitespace-only separator lines, empty text, trailing spaces, long words after existing words).

Decisions the plan didn't specify:
- Whitespace-only lines are treated as blank paragraph separators.
- Single newlines inside a paragraph are reflowed as spaces, since only blank lines separate paragraphs.
- Consecutive blank lines collapse to a single blank line in the output; leading/trailing blank lines are dropped.

